  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "FV uses the linear route only at exact rate = 0, so tiny rates such as 1e-15 lose over 60% via rounded 1 + rate",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0 builds 20131 and 20430, FV(rate, nper, pmt, [pv], [type]) takes the linear form -(pv + pmt * nper) only when rate = 0 exactly. For any nonzero rate, it computes factor = POWER(RN53(RN64(1 + rate)), nper), divides (factor - 1) / rate in x87 before multiplying by timing 1 + rate * type, and flushes each cashflow product before summing. At rate = 1e-15, nper = 10, pmt = -120, pv = 1000, type = 0, rounding 1 + 1e-15 in binary64 turns (factor - 1)/rate into ~11.102 instead of 10, returning 332.2676295501767 instead of the mathematical value ~200.0000000000054.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured in CalcFunc-Evidence cache/oracle/build-20131/FV.jsonl.gz (Excel 16.0 build 20131) and DnaCalc ported financial_time_value_family.rs (1,306/1,308 FV bank rows matched; 2 remaining under an open beginning-term pair).",
